(include-obligations (path "profiles/rv64gc-lab-v0/contract-v0.obligations.sexp"))
(include-obligations (path "profiles/rv64gc-lab-v0/contract-v1.obligations.sexp"))
(obligation (id "OB-GC-M") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v2") (contract_version "2") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The M extension's 13 forms compute as the pinned chapter defines them: MUL places the lower XLEN bits of the product in rd; MULH, MULHSU and MULHU the upper XLEN bits of the full 2xXLEN-bit product, signed x signed, signed x unsigned and unsigned x unsigned; DIV and DIVU divide rounding towards zero, and REM and REMU give the corresponding remainder, a nonzero signed remainder taking the dividend's sign; the RV64 word forms MULW, DIVW, DIVUW, REMW and REMUW operate on the lower 32 bits and sign-extend the 32-bit result, including on a divide by zero; division by zero yields a quotient with all bits set and a remainder equal to the dividend, and signed overflow (the most-negative integer divided by -1) a quotient equal to the dividend and a remainder of zero - no M instruction raises an exception.") (authority architecture) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-M") (locator "11.1.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-M") (locator "11.1.2")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-GC-M"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-GC-M") (required_checks "CHK-GC-M-POS") (required_checks "CHK-GC-M-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-GC-C") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v2") (contract_version "2") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The RV64+D C selection has 37 sixteen-bit forms, Zca plus Zcd. Each executes its declared single base-instruction expansion over the reconstructed compact registers and signed/scaled immediates; C.JALR takes its target from the old source and writes pc+2, including rd=rs1. Instruction PCs advance by two or four bytes under IALIGN=16. HINTs preserve architectural state except advancing PC and applicable performance counters, and C.EBREAK delivers breakpoint cause 3. Compressed D memory obeys the D extension and FS gate. Reserved operands are refused with their original sixteen bits under the declared illegal-instruction policy. Fetch reads the first parcel exactly and a second only for a 32-bit instruction; a second-parcel translation fault reports that parcel VA in xtval and the instruction start in xepc, before any instruction effect. The all-ones illegal instruction retains all ILEN=32 bits in the diagnostic. Valid C forms preserve the constrained LR/SC guarantee.") (authority architecture) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-C") (locator "27.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-C") (locator "27.1.4")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-C") (locator "27.1.6")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-MACHINE") (locator "2.1.1.15")) (parameters (param (name requirement_id) (value (str "REQ-GC-C"))) (param (name source_semantics) (value (str "defined")))) (dependencies "REQ-GC-C") (required_checks "CHK-GC-C-POS") (required_checks "CHK-GC-C-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-GC-ENV-FETCH-SUPPLY") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v2") (contract_version "2") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction environment-assumption) (statement "For every FetchParcel request the environment supplies exactly sixteen bits from the addressed executable physical region, or its declared access failure. It issues no unrequested fetch and fetches have no side effects. The CPU chooses necessary parcels under OB-GC-C. The witness counts each physical parcel request, including refused requests; a translation fault that prevents the request contributes zero. No speculative four-byte read or partial-success response is substituted.") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-INTRO") (locator "Memory")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-C") (locator "27.1")) (parameters (param (name fetch_width_bits) (value (int 16))) (param (name extraneous_fetch_permitted) (value (false))) (param (name fetch_side_effects) (value (str "none")))) (dependencies "OB-GC-C") (dependencies "OB-GC-ENV-TRANSLATION-INPUTS") (required_checks "CHK-GC-ENV-FETCH-SUPPLY-POS") (required_checks "CHK-GC-ENV-FETCH-SUPPLY-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-GC-FP-QUALIFIED-V2") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v2") (contract_version "2") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "The selected floating-point backend is the qualified rustc_apfloat 0.2.3+llvm-462a31f5a5ab, required as =0.2.3 and artifact-pinned by Cargo.lock, behind the RISC-V model layer crates/semulith-core/src/fp.rs. The qualification decision and closing measurement record finite evidence, including the model layer's corrections to overflow and underflow flags. F and D are implemented; their numeric and instruction guarantees retain their own checks. Sail and Spike share SoftFloat numeric ancestry, so their agreement is encoding/state evidence and never two independent numeric implementations. Supersedes the pre-qualification condition in OB-FP-DEFER; CPU acceptance still depends on every remaining gate.") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-F") (locator "20.1.4")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-D") (locator "21.1.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-PSABI") (locator "§2.4–§2.5")) (parameters (param (name supersedes) (value (str "OB-FP-DEFER"))) (param (name backend) (value (str "rustc_apfloat"))) (param (name backend_requirement) (value (str "=0.2.3"))) (param (name backend_artifact) (value (str "0.2.3+llvm-462a31f5a5ab"))) (param (name model_layer) (value (str "crates/semulith-core/src/fp.rs"))) (param (name qualification_record) (value (str "docs/decisions/decision_fp-backend-qualification.md"))) (param (name closing_record) (value (str "docs/decisions/reference_fp-model-layer-acceptance.md"))) (param (name sail_spike_numeric_independent) (value (false)))) (required_checks "CHK-GC-FP-QUALIFIED-V2-POS") (required_checks "CHK-GC-FP-QUALIFIED-V2-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-GC-DEFINITION-V2") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v2") (contract_version "2") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "This unit uses the generated-definition vehicle. Its encoding composition is complete for the declared profile scope, with no unbound slots; the canonical state, encoding/semantics and guest corpus own the generated state_rv64gc.rs, definition_rv64gc.rs and guests_rv64gc.rs mirrors. The owner generators and their drift gates govern those mirrors. This replaces both the original profile-resolution stage and the later partial-composition checkpoint, without fixing the current contract to obsolete slot or guest counts. Selection and generated-route consistency are scope evidence; instruction behavior is established separately by executable checks.") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-INTRO") (locator "RISC-V Software Execution Environments and Harts")) (parameters (param (name supersedes) (value (strs "OB-RESOLUTION-ROUTE" "OB-ROUTE-FLIP"))) (param (name vehicle) (value (str "generated-definition"))) (param (name composition) (value (str "complete")))) (dependencies "OB-GC-COMPOSITION") (dependencies "OB-SCOPE-CENSUS") (required_checks "CHK-GC-DEFINITION-V2-POS") (required_checks "CHK-GC-DEFINITION-V2-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-GC-FAULT-PRIORITY-V2") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v2") (contract_version "2") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction cpu-guarantee) (statement "Synchronous exception selection follows the in-scope projection of the pinned priority table: the first encountered instruction-translation page/access fault, then physical instruction access failure, then decode/illegal-instruction and environment-call/break outcomes, then the selected high-priority data alignment check before explicit-access translation, then its first encountered translation fault and finally physical data access failure. Ordinary misaligned data accesses use causes 4/6; misaligned LR uses cause 5 and SC/AMO cause 7 at that same pre-translation point. Sdtrig instruction/data address triggers are absent; this does not exclude environment-break exceptions. EBREAK and C.EBREAK deliver cause 3, with the instruction start in xepc and xtval. Architecturally produced control-flow targets obey IALIGN=16. The priority, FS-Off and breakpoint fixtures witness the selected cases; finite testing is not universal proof of every exception combination.") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-MACHINE") (locator "§2.1.1.15")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-A") (locator "12.1.2")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-A") (locator "12.1.4")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-C") (locator "27.1.5.6")) (parameters (param (name supersedes) (value (str "OB-FAULT-PRIORITY"))) (param (name data_misalignment_priority) (value (str "before-translation"))) (param (name address_triggers) (value (false))) (param (name environment_break_cause) (value (int 3)))) (required_checks "CHK-GC-FAULT-PRIORITY-V2-POS") (required_checks "CHK-GC-FAULT-PRIORITY-V2-NEG"))
(obligation (id "OB-GC-ENV-ADDRESS-UNITS") (contract_id "rv64gc-lab-env-v2") (contract_version "2") (profile_ids "rv64gc-lab-v0") (direction environment-assumption) (statement "Every environment request address is a 64-bit unsigned physical address measured in 8-bit bytes, including FetchParcel, Load, Store and WalkAccess. The CPU translates guest virtual instruction/data addresses before crossing this boundary; page-table reads already name physical addresses. Bare mode uses the identity mapping. The environment interprets the entire supplied byte address: no host pointer, word index, 32-bit truncation or guest VA substitutes for it. Address arithmetic by the CPU wraps at XLEN; a request spanning an undeclared physical region fails under the memory-map contract rather than wrapping through that region. The direct fixture observes nonzero offsets and physical addresses above 32 bits; deliberately distorted addresses report a typed contract violation, while a declared physical access failure remains a target exception.") (authority laboratory) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-INTRO") (locator "Memory")) (source_refs (source_id "RVI-RVWMO") (locator "17.1")) (source_refs (source_id "RVP-SUPERVISOR") (locator "11.1.4.1")) (parameters (param (name address_bits) (value (int 64))) (param (name address_unit_bits) (value (int 8))) (param (name request_address_space) (value (str "physical"))) (param (name host_pointer_substitution) (value (false))) (param (name word_index_substitution) (value (false)))) (dependencies "OB-ADDRESS-SPACE") (dependencies "OB-GC-ENV-TRANSLATION-INPUTS") (required_checks "CHK-GC-ENV-ADDRESS-UNITS-POS") (required_checks "CHK-GC-ENV-ADDRESS-UNITS-NEG"))
